{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Random Forest Classification.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Random Forest Classification.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"random forest classification random forest classification","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Random Forest Classification.md","fileName":"Random Forest Classification.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Random Forest Classification","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 21:00\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Ensemble and Semi-Supervised Classification]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Ensemble and Semi-Supervised Classification","Out-of-Bag Error","dataclassification.pdf","essentialsofdatascience.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Random Forest Classification.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Random Forest Classification.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"random forest classification random forest classification","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Random Forest Classification.md","fileName":"Random Forest Classification.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Random Forest Classification","heading":"Random Forest Classification","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Random forest classification combines decision trees trained on bootstrap samples while considering a random subset of features at each split. Both sources of randomness promote diversity among the trees.\n\nThe final class is chosen by aggregate voting. Deep individual trees can fit complex patterns, while averaging reduces their variance; restricting candidate features prevents a few dominant predictors from making every tree too similar.\n\nThe book fits hundreds of randomized trees, monitors [[Out-of-Bag Error]], and examines variable importance before evaluating held-out probabilities. The gap between near-perfect training performance and weaker validation performance remains evidence that ensemble accuracy must be checked independently.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Ensemble and Semi-Supervised Classification","Out-of-Bag Error","dataclassification.pdf","essentialsofdatascience.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Random Forest Classification.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Random Forest Classification.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"random forest classification random forest classification","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Random Forest Classification.md","fileName":"Random Forest Classification.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Random Forest Classification","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[dataclassification.pdf]]\n\n[[essentialsofdatascience.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Ensemble and Semi-Supervised Classification","Out-of-Bag Error","dataclassification.pdf","essentialsofdatascience.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}